    memory: 'Base weights once; each adapter costs `r × (d_in + d_out) × bytes` per adapted matrix, typically tens to a few hundred MB; the adapter cache bounds how many are resident.',
    compute: 'Extra low-rank matmuls per token, small relative to the base at moderate rank; the gather kernels are memory-bound and add a few percent to step time.',
    communication: 'Under TP the adapter matrices are sharded like their base matrices; adapter loads move from host to GPU on demand.',
